\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces NEMS feasibility and stability assessment for the rotational quantum clutch in true vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm  bg}=1.0$) at $T=300{}\text  { K}$. The four-panel benchmark quantifies (1) room-temperature Matsubara dispersion across PEC ($0\text  { K}$), Gold ($0\text  { K}$), and Gold ($300\text  { K}$); (2) net repulsive restoring force under uncompensated electrostatic bias/patch voltages; (3) radial Casimir stiffness versus the $\text  {Si}\langle 110\rangle $ mechanical flexure suspension stiffness; and (4) repulsive lift and switching swing across lithographic critical-dimension ($\Delta \text  {CD}$) tooth-width etch tolerances.}}{21}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
